  "title": "Unique Characteristics of Surah al-Tawhid & 100 Ayahs from the Quran",
  "data": "Shaykh al-Kulayni, in al-Kafi, has quoted Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) as saying, “My father used to say: [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) is a third of the Qur'an and [Surah al-Kafirun](A113) is a quarter.”\nImam Musa al-Kazim (a.s.) is reported to have said, “Whoever recites [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) before going to sleep will be saved from hemiplegia (paralysis of one side of the body), by the permission of Allah. Whoever recites it after each obligatory prayer will not be harmed by any creature that stings.”\nImam al-Kazim (a.s.) is also reported to have said, “Whoever places (the recitation of) Surah al-Tawhid between himself and any tyrant, Almighty Allah will save him from that tyrant. Whoever recites Surah al-Tawhid in front of him, behind him, to his right and to his left, Almighty Allah will grant him its good and keep its evil from reaching him.”\nImam al-Kazim (a.s.) is also reported to have said: If you fear something, recite any one hundred verses of the Holy Qur'an and then say three times:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اكْشِفْ عَنِّى الْبَلَاۤءَ\nALLAAHUMMAK SHIF A'NNIL BALAA'\nO Allah, remove the affliction from me.\nShaykh al-Kulayni, in al-Kafi, has quoted Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) as saying, “Whoever believes in Allah and in the Last Day must not neglect reciting Surah al-Tawhid after each obligatory prayer, because whoever recites it, Almighty Allah will give him the good of this world and the good of the Hereafter, and will forgive him, his parents and his children.”\nImam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is also reported to have said, “Whoever recites [Surah al-Takathur](A106) (No. 102) before going to sleep will be saved from the trial of the grave.”"
}
